Spec: Project/Modules

Purpose:
  Declare each generic module in the SDDRA ecosystem — what it owns,
  its public API surface, and its direct dependencies. Modules are the
  deployable/code-boundary units that implement domains.

Rules:
  A module MUST declare what it owns.
  A module MUST declare its public API surface.
  A module MUST explicitly declare its dependencies (`deps`).
  A module MUST NOT depend on any module not listed in its declared deps.
  A module MAY declare `files` (owned source paths) — routing pointers only.
  A module MAY declare `tests` (owned test paths) — routing pointers only.
  A module MAY declare `bounded_contexts` when a domain spans multiple implementations.

Modules:

  integration-module:
    purpose: External system integration with config-driven field mapping and retry
    domain: Integration
    bounded_contexts:
      - http-client (external API communication)
      - field-mapping (request/response transformation)
      - pre-check (identity validation)
      - status-polling (application status tracking)
      - webhook-processing (incoming webhook handling)
    owns:
      - HTTP client configuration (base_url, timeout, auth, content_type)
      - Request field mapping and transformation
      - Response field mapping and transformation
      - Retry policy (max_attempts, backoff, dead-letter)
      - Audit log (request/response/execution_time)
      - Pre-check execution (optional, config-driven)
      - Status polling (optional, config-driven)
      - Webhook processing (optional, signature validation)
      - Daily limit enforcement
    api:
      - execute(integration, payload) -> {success, data, error}
      - executePreCheck(integration, values) -> {passed, message}
      - checkStatus(integration, externalId) -> {status, code}
      - processWebhook(integrationName, data) -> {mapped_fields}
    deps:
      - external-api (third-party service)
      - database (persistence)
      - cache (rate limits, config)
    files:
      - src/integration/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/integration/**/*
    state: active

  event-processor:
    purpose: Event/message intake, dispatch, and lifecycle management
    domain: EventProcessing
    bounded_contexts:
      - websocket-ingestion (real-time event intake)
      - queue-consumer (async message processing)
      - polling-fallback (DB-based queue fallback)
    owns:
      - Event claiming and deduplication
      - Handler dispatch (service + event_type routing)
      - Retry policy (count, backoff, dead-letter)
      - Correlation ID tracking
      - Batch completion and status updates
    api:
      - claim(batchSize) -> [eventRows]
      - handle(eventRow) -> {status, result}
      - complete(eventId, status, retryCount) -> void
      - completeBatch(updates) -> void
    deps:
      - message-broker (RabbitMQ/Kafka)
      - database (event persistence)
      - cache (deduplication, rate limits)
    files:
      - src/event/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/event/**/*
    state: active

  notification-service:
    purpose: Multi-channel outbound messaging
    domain: Notification
    bounded_contexts:
      - email (template rendering and delivery)
      - sms (provider abstraction)
      - telegram (bot API)
      - slack (webhook-based rich messages)
    owns:
      - Template engine (placeholder replacement, HTML rendering)
      - Provider abstraction (send via configured channel)
      - Daily limits per integration
      - Retry logic for failed sends
    api:
      - send(integration, payload) -> {success, log_id, error}
      - queue(integration, payload) -> {queued, request_id}
      - retry(logId) -> {success, error}
      - renderTemplate(templateName, data) -> renderedContent
    deps:
      - email-provider (Mailgun/SMTP)
      - messaging-provider (Slack/Telegram/SMS)
      - database (notification log)
      - cache (template cache)
    files:
      - src/notification/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/notification/**/*
    state: active

  scheduled-sync:
    purpose: Periodic and delayed task execution
    domain: Scheduling
    bounded_contexts:
      - cron-jobs (periodic external sync)
      - delayed-tasks (batch operations)
    owns:
      - Cron job registration and execution
      - Delayed task queue management
      - Batch orchestration (pre-check, sync)
    api:
      - registerCron(schedule, handler) -> jobId
      - executeDelayed(task) -> void
      - getJobStatus(jobId) -> {status, result}
    deps:
      - integration-module (external API calls)
      - event-processor (async processing)
      - database (job state)
    files:
      - src/scheduling/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/scheduling/**/*
    state: active

  user-service:
    purpose: User identity and profile management
    domain: User
    bounded_contexts:
      - profile (core user attributes)
      - identity-mapping (cross-system ID mapping)
    owns:
      - User profile data
      - External service user mapping (internal ID -> external ID)
      - User-level daily limits
    api:
      - getProfile(userId) -> UserProfile
      - updateProfile(userId, attributes) -> void
      - mapExternalId(userId, externalId, provider) -> void
      - resolveInternalId(externalId) -> userId
    deps:
      - database (user storage)
      - cache (profile cache)
    files:
      - src/user/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/user/**/*
    state: active

  gamification-module:
    purpose: Gamification platform integration — points, badges, leaderboards, rules
    domain: Gamification
    bounded_contexts:
      - rules-engine (declarative rule evaluation)
      - leaderboard (ranked lists, scopes, caching)
      - player-profile (player profile, external identity, progression)
      - anti-cheat (validation, anomaly detection, rollback)
    owns:
      - Rule definitions and evaluation engine
      - Point award processing (idempotent, auditable)
      - Badge unlock evaluation
      - Leaderboard write/read models
      - Player profile sync and identity mapping
      - Anti-cheat detection and enforcement
      - Real-time event delivery
      - Scheduled batch jobs (leaderboard rebuild, badge evaluation)
    api:
      - evaluateRules(event, userState) -> {actions}
      - getLeaderboard(scope, page) -> {entries}
      - getUserRank(userId, scope) -> {rank, score}
      - getPlayerProfile(userId) -> PlayerProfile
      - syncPlayerProfile(userId) -> void
      - awardPoints(userId, amount, reason) -> PointEvent
      - unlockBadge(userId, badgeId) -> BadgeEvent
    deps:
      - external-api (third-party gamification service)
      - database (persistence)
      - cache (sorted sets, rate limits)
      - message-broker (async event processing)
    files:
      - src/gamification/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/gamification/**/*
    state: active

  matchmaking-module:
    purpose: Queue-based matchmaking and session formation
    domain: Matchmaking
    bounded_contexts:
      - queue-management (ticket enqueue, cancel, poll)
      - session-formation (match creation, late join)
      - game-config (durable config, runtime projection)
    owns:
      - Queue and ticket management
      - Session formation and late join
      - Game configuration CRUD
      - Matchmaking engine
      - Latency-based compatibility matching
    api:
      - enqueue(gameId, playerId, region, latencyMs) -> Ticket
      - getTicket(gameId, ticketId) -> Ticket
      - cancelTicket(gameId, ticketId) -> void
      - getSession(sessionId) -> Session
      - lateJoin(sessionId, playerId) -> Session
      - upsertGameConfig(gameId, config) -> GameConfig
      - getGameConfig(gameId) -> GameConfig
    deps:
      - database (durable config)
      - cache (queues, sessions, locks)
      - orm (data access)
    files:
      - src/matchmaking/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/matchmaking/**/*
    state: active

Rules:
  [M1] A module MUST declare all direct dependencies.
  [M2] A module MUST NOT depend on another module's internal structures.
  [M3] A module's public API is its contract — internal implementation may change.
  [M4] A module MAY implement multiple bounded contexts from one or more domains.
  [M5] A module's `files` and `tests` declarations are routing pointers, not source of truth.
  [M6] A module MUST be independently testable.
  [M7] A module SHOULD be independently deployable when service extraction is needed.
  [M8] Module boundaries MUST align with domain boundaries.

Navigation:
  Domains: @domains.sdd
  Flows: @flows.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/principles.sdd

State: +
